            "review_title": "Review at Hang Duong Quan Restaurant",
            "review_text": "spktravels\nTallman, New York360 contributions\n1\nRustic water front restaurant\nMay 2019 • Couples\nOnce again I was the only foreigner in this restaurant which is always a good sign\n\nAt lunch the common theme seemed to be tables of local men consuming vast quantities of Tiger beer and smoking. The waitresses were anxious to bring them more and more beer. \n\nBut we were there for the food. Sitting at a table along the River we enjoyed calamari, clams with onions and peanuts and finally a well prepared lobster. \n\nService was efficient.\nRead more\nWritten May 17, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
